{"abstract":"Plants defend themselves against attack by natural enemies, and these defenses vary widely across populations. However, whether communities of natural enemies are a sufficiently potent force to maintain polymorphisms in defensive traits is largely unknown. Here, we exploit the genetic resources of Arabidopsis thaliana, coupled with 39 years of field data on aphid abundance, to (i) demonstrate that geographic patterns in a polymorphic defense locus (GS-ELONG) are strongly correlated with changes in the relative abundance of two specialist aphids; and (ii) demonstrate differential selection by the two aphids on GS-ELONG, using a multigeneration selection experiment. We thereby show a causal link between variation in abundance of the two specialist aphids and the geographic pattern at GS-ELONG, which highlights the potency of natural enemies as selective forces.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Zuest, Tobias","Heichinger, Christian","Grossniklaus, Ueli","Harrington, Richard","Kliebenstein, Daniel James","Turnbull, Lindsay A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-528097"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Rothamsted Research","University of Zurich"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"natural enemies drive geographic variation in plant defenses","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226397","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-528097","identifier":[{"id":"23042895","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84867193262","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e1575420-7ce2-4b09-97c5-f20e999f9d97"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FDA591ACF55F01C126D23FC3FBE2E417"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226397","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"university of zurich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Zurich","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"rothamsted research","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Rothamsted Research","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Plant Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias","key":"zuestpau","last":"Zuest","name":"Zuest, Tobias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"heichingerpau","last":"Heichinger","name":"Heichinger, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ueli","key":"grossniklauspau","last":"Grossniklaus","name":"Grossniklaus, Ueli","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Richard","key":"harringtonpau","last":"Harrington","name":"Harrington, Richard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel James","key":"kliebensteinpau","last":"Kliebenstein","locid":"25be328a-e84c-45c1-abd6-5ebcd56bf5cc","name":"Kliebenstein, Daniel James","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lindsay A.","key":"turnbullpau","last":"Turnbull","name":"Turnbull, Lindsay A.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23042895"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1126/science.1226397","issn":["00368075","10959203"],"issn_org":["00368075"],"issue":"6103","journal":"Science","pages":"116-119","status":"p","title":"Science","volume":"338"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84867193262"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e1575420-7ce2-4b09-97c5-f20e999f9d97"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Natural enemies drive geographic variation in plant defenses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-528097","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
